<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>
    {%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
      {%- comment -%} Fallback for when the homepage title preference is unset or domain-only. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if page_title == blank or page_title == 'BRAND-DOMAIN' or page_title == shop.name -%}
        BRAND | Women's Fashion
      {%- else -%}
        {{- page_title -}}
        {%- unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {{- page_title -}}
      {%- if current_tags %} &ndash; {{ current_tags | join: ', ' }}{% endif -%}
      {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; {{ 'general.title_page' | t: page: current_page }}{% endif -%}
      {%- unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </title>
  {%- if page_description -%}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
  {%- elsif request.page_type == 'index' -%}
    <meta name="description" content="BRAND — women's fashion with free shipping and 30-day returns.">
  {%- endif -%}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
  {% render 'social-meta' %}
  {%- comment -%} Favicon files are generated from the logo — never hand-edit. {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{ 'brand-favicon.svg' | asset_url }}">
  {%- comment -%} PNG fallback: mobile/in-app browsers + iOS don't take SVG favicons {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="{{ 'brand-favicon-32.png' | asset_url }}">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="{{ 'brand-touch-180.png' | asset_url }}">
  {%- comment -%} Archivo covers --font-display AND --font-ui too (see @font-face + :root
  below) — the Prata preload stays because .pdp__color ("in <Colour>") is still Prata
  italic and sits above the fold on every PDP. {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'prata-regular.woff2' | asset_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  {%- comment -%} Archivo: now the whole UI/display/prose voice (regular + italic); the
  500 weight rides the same variable file as regular (see @font-face below), no
  third preload needed. {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'archivo-var.woff2' | asset_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'archivo-400i.woff2' | asset_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  {%- if template.name == 'product' and product.featured_media.media_type == 'image' -%}
    {%- comment -%} ceiling 1024w. The URLs MUST mirror the gallery's exactly (500 / 800 / 1024,
    width only, no height, no crop) — any difference and the CDN hands back a different URL than
    the gallery renders, so the hero image downloads twice. height+crop is avoided here: the
    source images are mixed formats (only 23% are true 2:3) and cropping them costs real garment
    detail. Keep in sync with sections/main-product.liquid when the PDP stage writes it. {%- endcomment -%}
    <link rel="preload" as="image"
      href="{{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 800 }}"
      imagesrcset="{{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 500 }} 500w, {{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w, {{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 1024 }} 1024w"
      imagesizes="(max-width: 720px) 80vw, 46vw"
      fetchpriority="high">
  {%- endif -%}
  <style>
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'Prata';
      src: url('{{ 'prata-regular.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
      font-weight: 400;
      font-style: normal;
      font-display: swap;
    }
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'Prata-fallback';
      src: local('Georgia'), local('Times New Roman');
      size-adjust: 104%;
      ascent-override: 98%;
    }
    {%- comment -%} archivo-var.woff2 is the full variable file (fvar wght 100-900,
    confirmed via fontTools) but the @font-face range below is what the browser actually
    maps CSS font-weight onto — set to "400 700" so the six font-weight:600 call sites
    (.pdp__name, .pdp__rb-name, .acc__q, prose h4/strong) render as real Archivo Semibold
    instead of clamping to 500. No new file fetch: the weight is already in the download. {%- endcomment -%}
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'Archivo';
      src: url('{{ 'archivo-var.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
      font-weight: 400 700;
      font-style: normal;
      font-display: swap;
    }
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'Archivo';
      src: url('{{ 'archivo-400i.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
      font-weight: 400;
      font-style: italic;
      font-display: swap;
    }
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'Archivo-fallback';
      src: local('Helvetica Neue'), local('Arial');
      size-adjust: 100%;
    }
    :root {
      --paper: {{ settings.color_paper }};
      --ink: {{ settings.color_ink }};
      --cream: {{ settings.color_cream }};
      --hairline: {{ settings.color_hairline }};
      --mute: {{ settings.color_mute }};
      {%- comment -%} --font-display uses Prata (serif) for display headings (.dxl/.dl/.dm
      — hero, category typo-block, editorial captions, footer newsletter headline);
      --font-ui and --font-prose stay Archivo (labels, buttons, nav, prose, bullets keep
      the grotesque voice). {%- endcomment -%}
      --font-display: 'Prata', 'Prata-fallback', Georgia, serif;
      --font-ui: 'Archivo', 'Archivo-fallback', 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      {%- comment -%} The only Prata holdout: the short italic tags under the product name
      (.pdp__color, .pdp__descriptor, .pdp__rb-sub in theme.css). No other selector may
      reference this var. {%- endcomment -%}
      --font-accent-italic: 'Prata', 'Prata-fallback', Georgia, serif;
      {%- comment -%} the only place a warm tone may appear, and only when settings.buy_color selects it {%- endcomment -%}
      --buy-fill: {% if settings.buy_color == 'amber' %}{{ settings.color_amber }}{% else %}var(--ink){% endif %};
      {%- comment -%} buy-text vs accent fill: check contrast against color_amber (WCAG >= 4.5) when customizing {%- endcomment -%}
    --buy-text: {% if settings.buy_color == 'amber' %}var(--paper){% else %}var(--paper){% endif %};
    }
  </style>
  {%- comment -%} The six *-extras.css files are combined into theme.css (in their
  original load order — cascade unchanged). One stylesheet = one render-blocking
  request instead of seven. New block styles can go into a separate extras file
  linked here, then get combined into theme.css again afterward. {%- endcomment -%}
  {{ 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <script>
    /* .reveal starts at opacity 0 — scoped to html.js so a browser without
       JavaScript (or with theme.js blocked) never gets a blank page. Set here,
       in the head, so the class is present before first paint. */
    document.documentElement.classList.add('js');
    window.Theme = {
      moneyFormat: {{ shop.money_format | json }},
      cartAddUrl: '{{ routes.cart_add_url }}.js',
      cartChangeUrl: '{{ routes.cart_change_url }}.js',
      cartUrl: '{{ routes.cart_url }}.js',
      searchUrl: '{{ routes.predictive_search_url }}',
      recommendationsUrl: '{{ routes.product_recommendations_url }}',
      t: {
        optionColor: {{ 'product.option_color' | t | json }},
        optionSize: {{ 'product.option_size' | t | json }},
        selectSize: {{ 'product.atc.select_size' | t | json }},
        unavailable: {{ 'product.atc.unavailable' | t | json }},
        addToBag: {{ 'product.atc.add_to_bag' | t | json }},
        soldOut: {{ 'product.atc.sold_out' | t | json }},
        selectSizeAria: {{ 'product.atc.select_size_aria' | t | json }},
        added: {{ 'product.atc.added' | t | json }},
        cartError: {{ 'cart.errors.generic' | t | json }},
        optionUnavailable: {{ 'cart.errors.option_unavailable' | t | json }},
        chooseSize: {{ 'product.complete_look.choose_size' | t | json }},
        optionSelect: {{ 'product.option_select' | t | json }},
        addShort: {{ 'cart.cross.add_short' | t | json }}
        {%- comment %} disabled: almostSoldOut/sellingFast/inStock backed S.scarcityFor/S.applyScarcity (id-modulo pseudo-scarcity); every caller is now disabled in snippets/pdp-scarcity.liquid, quick-view.liquid, cart-miniview.liquid, so this data only leaked unused strings into page source with nothing left to read it. Re-enable only with real inventory gating. {% endcomment -%}
      }
    };
  </script>
  <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>
  {%- comment -%} New behaviour ships in its own module per block instead of growing theme.js,
  so multiple contributors never touch the same JS file. theme.js keeps every cart invariant
  and the PDP variant logic — these two only ADD. {%- endcomment -%}
  <script src="{{ 'pdp-extras.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>
  <script src="{{ 'cart-extras.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>
  {%- comment -%} swatch → card image preview; purely additive, the swatch is a
  working variant link without it {%- endcomment -%}
  <script src="{{ 'card-extras.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>
  <script src="{{ 'standard-extras.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>
  {%- comment -%} Rendered from the layout, not from main-product: the snippet also holds the
  Organization + WebSite blocks, which are gated on template.name == 'index'. {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'jsonld' %}
  {% render 'gtag' %}
  {{ content_for_header }}
  <script type="speculationrules">
    {
      "prefetch": [{
        "where": {
          "and": [
            { "href_matches": "/*" },
            { "not": { "href_matches": "/cart*" } },
            { "not": { "href_matches": "/checkout*" } },
            { "not": { "href_matches": "/account*" } }
          ]
        },
        "eagerness": "moderate"
      }]
    }
  </script>
</head>
<body class="template-{{ template.name | handle }}">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">{{ 'layout.skip_to_content' | t }}</a>
  {% sections 'header-group' %}
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
    {%- comment -%} No PDP breadcrumb anywhere. The layout copy was removed, and the
    bottom .pdp__crumbs nav in sections/main-product.liquid was deleted along with its
    styles. Do not reintroduce either one. {%- endcomment -%}
  </main>
  {% sections 'footer-group' %}
  {%- comment -%} The floating search pill was removed. The header's search icon
  and /search are the search entry points. Do not reintroduce snippets/search-bar.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'cart-drawer' %}
  {% render 'quick-view' %}
  {%- comment -%} Newsletter popup is toggle-owned via settings.newsletter_popup_enabled
  so it can be switched on or off per store. theme.js guards on #nl-popup being absent,
  so the toggle is safe. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if settings.newsletter_popup_enabled -%}
    {% render 'newsletter-popup' %}
  {%- endif -%}
</body>
</html>
